STABLE
------
== Drop support for PostgreSQL versions before 12
extension_drop depends on cat_tools, which already requires PostgreSQL
12+. A fresh install of extension_drop was already broken below that
too (a cat_tools function it calls needs PG11+ internally) -- this
just makes the declared floor honest.

== Require USAGE for PUBLIC on the extension's schema
`CREATE EXTENSION` and `ALTER EXTENSION ... UPDATE` now fail unless `PUBLIC`
has USAGE on the schema extension_drop is installed in, and new event
triggers protect that USAGE afterwards. See README.md for details.

== Pin every function's search_path to pg_catalog
All functions set `search_path = pg_catalog, pg_temp` and qualify their own
objects with the extension's schema, so a role with CREATE on that schema
can't plant operators or functions that they run. Registered SQL runs with
`search_path = pg_catalog, <extension's schema>, pg_temp`: the schemas of
extensions extension_drop requires (such as cat_tools) are no longer on it,
so registered SQL that uses them must qualify them. CREATE on the extension's
schema remains trusted for registered SQL, which resolves names on its path
there.

== Run drop commands when `DROP SCHEMA ... CASCADE` or `DROP OWNED BY` drops an extension
The event trigger now fires for `DROP SCHEMA` and `DROP OWNED` as well as
`DROP EXTENSION`. Previously the other two commands left a stale registration
that made every later `DROP EXTENSION` fail with `XD001`; remove any with
`extension_drop__repair()`. Any role that can drop an extension can do so
without privileges on extension_drop's table; the registered SQL runs as that
role, in extension-name order when one command drops several.
`extension_drop__sanity_assert()` now runs inside `extension_drop__claim()`,
before the registered SQL. See README.md.

== Fix `extension_drop__update()` and `extension_drop__remove()` with several registrations
With more than one extension registered, they changed every registration
instead of only the named one.

== Remove redundant client_min_messages handling from install script
`CREATE EXTENSION` already raises `client_min_messages` to `WARNING` for
the install script (only-raising, so a stricter caller is respected) and
restores it afterward, so the script's own save/restore was redundant --
and being blind to the caller's level, it could actually lower a
stricter caller's `client_min_messages` during install.

== Mark release as stable
No functional issues turned up in the 9+ years since 0.1.1; promoting
from `testing` to `stable`.

0.1.1
-----
Fix extension dependencies.

0.1.0
-----
Initial release.
